# Implementation Plan - Industrial Stabilization & Visibility

This plan resolves the "Stalled Dashboard" issue and replaces hardcoded progress labels with real-time, calculated metrics for 1.8GB+ industrial SQL processing.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Visibility Regression**: I identified that the "TABLES" and "ROWS" cards are currently showing "Skeletons" (gray bars) instead of numbers during the restoration phase. I will remove this block so you can see every single table as it is created.
> 
> **Progress Calculation**: I will switch from a hardcoded 45% to a real-time calculation: `(Decompressed MB / Total MB) * 100`.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend - Search Path Fix

#### [MODIFY] [service.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- Explicitly set the database `search_path` to include `public` during the watcher loop. This fixes the "relation jobs does not exist" error that was stalling the increments.

### 2. Frontend - Dynamic Progress

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/app/page.tsx)
- **Remove Skeletons**: Change the SummaryCard logic to show the current incrementing values even while the job status is `restoring`.
- **Calculated Readiness**: Update `getReadiness` to use `metadata.data_processed_mb` and `activeJob.file_size`.
- **Decompression Label**: Show `X% - Decompressing & Streaming...` in the Readiness card.

### 3. Frontend - Time remaining

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/app/page.tsx)
- Add a refined time-remaining calculation for the restoration phase.

## Open Questions

- **Polling Frequency**: Currently, we check the DB every 10 seconds. For a 1.8GB file, this is safe. Would you like it faster (e.g., 5 seconds) for more "fluid" numbers?

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Verify that `sqauto_api` logs no longer show `UndefinedTable` errors.
- Verify that the API response for `/jobs/{id}` contains `data_processed_mb`.

### Manual Verification
- I will start a 1.8GB restoration and provide a walkthrough showing the TABLES and ROWS cards incrementing from 0 to final counts in real-time.
